# Cargo.lock IS tracked. It was ignored while this was a workspace of
# libraries with no dependencies; now that the `pbr_cube` example exists and
# the tree pins a 0.x shader compiler (`wesl`, see ADR 0003), a reproducible
# build for CI and for anyone running the demo is worth more than letting
# consumers resolve freely — which a library consumer does anyway, since
# Cargo ignores a dependency's lockfile.

# Output the demo writes when `--out` is not given.
